---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Math from '../components/Math.astro';
import { SITE, isoDate } from '../consts';
import { publishedEntries } from '../lib/entries';
import shearSvg from '../figures/shear-grid.svg?raw';

const entries = await publishedEntries();

/* The register of avenues. States and gaps for the first three rows are taken
   from jc2-lean's own README so the page does not overstate them; the rest are
   placeholders to be confirmed against AUDIT.md before this goes live. */
const avenues = [
  {
    n: '01',
    name: 'Three mechanisms from degree cells',
    state: 'Proved · Lean',
    level: 'proved',
    gap: 'Theorem A, the vertex gap, and the cube-root grading, each found in one cell and machine-checked there. The laboratory phase. The all-degree program below is built from them and from what the census taught.',
    href: '/entries/polynomial-ode-rigidity',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    name: 'The census never empties',
    state: 'Theorem',
    level: 'proved',
    gap: 'Three unbounded families pass every printed condition, so no degree bound can come from the numerical skeleton. Promoted at the skeleton level; the ray with N pinned at 6 is provisional. Geometric realisation of any member is not claimed.',
    href: '/entries/census-never-empties',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    name: 'Trace and moment identities',
    state: 'Proved · not a ceiling',
    level: 'proved',
    gap: 'The identities are true with no Keller hypothesis and were promoted with repairs. Their degree bound is attained, so they give a shape constraint on (e, q_max), vacuous on the frontier. What survived: a one-trace Keller test and exact remainder arithmetic for the interpolation engine.',
    href: '/entries/trace-identity',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    name: 'Moh\'s descent and theorem (T)',
    state: 'Partial',
    level: 'partial',
    gap: 'Descent to monomial-Jacobian pairs is promoted, with an erratum to Moh\'s Appendix II. Theorem (T) is proved on the K = 16 ray through t = 8; the uniform statement is open. Residual at n up to 200: 64 necessary configurations. Brute force is exhausted on every chart family.',
    href: '/entries/moh-descent',
  },
  {
    n: '05',
    name: 'Galois orbits and the actual-stabilizer screen',
    state: 'Theorem',
    level: 'proved',
    gap: '(UNI) is not a theorem; the orbit-size law replaces it. The actual-stabilizer screen is promoted: 24,063 to 1,420 to 90 necessary configurations at n up to 200, and at n up to 100 it reproduces Moh\'s printed list exactly. Nested packing above s = 3 is open.',
    href: '/entries/galois-orbits',
  },
  {
    n: '06',
    name: 'The curve of escaping values',
    state: 'Theorem',
    level: 'proved',
    gap: 'CUSP-A-VOID, integration #9: the non-properness set of a noninvertible Keller map is never homeomorphic to the complex line. Producer Opus, hostile gate GPT-5.5 all confirmed, countermodel arm all survive. Entry to follow.',
  },
];
---

<Base title="The Road to JC₂">
  <div class="prose">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>The Road to JC<sub>2</sub></h1>

      {/* PLACEHOLDER PROSE — DC to replace. Set exactly as the final copy will be. */}
      <p class="lede">
        A campaign to settle JC<sub>2</sub>, the last remaining part of the Jacobian
        conjecture. We show our work as we go: the mechanisms we can prove, the
        connections we find, the new ideas, and the approaches that failed.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure
      class="statement wide"
      role="figure"
      aria-label="Two panels sharing one coordinate frame. On the left, a square grid. On the right, its image under the shear: horizontal lines stay straight and slide sideways, while vertical lines bend into parabolas."
    >
      <div class="statement__plate" set:html={shearSvg} />
      <Math display tex={String.raw`F(x,y)=(x+y^{2},\,y)`} />
      <figcaption class="statement__gloss">
        A polynomial map with constant nonzero Jacobian. JC<sub>2</sub> says every such
        map is invertible.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      For a primer on the plane Jacobian conjecture, and why reversibility near every
      point does not obviously give a single global inverse, see{' '}
      <a href="/entries/background">Background</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What is left to do</h2>

    {/* States are as banked in AUDIT.md and the LIVE STATE of 2026-09-06. */}
    <div class="register">
      <ol>
        {avenues.map((a) => (
          <li class="register__row" data-level={a.level}>
            <span class="label register__n">{a.n}</span>
            <span class="register__name">
              {a.href ? <a href={a.href}>{a.name}</a> : a.name}
            </span>
            <span class="label register__state">{a.state}</span>
            <p class="register__gap">{a.gap}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    {/* PLACEHOLDER PROSE — DC to replace. */}
    <p class="terminus">
      This list is not closed. We are always looking for new avenues, and one that is not
      on it may well turn out to be the one that settles the problem. Finding a new line
      of attack counts as much as closing a gap in an existing one.
    </p>

    <h2>Contributing</h2>

    {/* PLACEHOLDER PROSE — DC to replace.
        Intended channel: open-source the root jc2/ repository, not jc2-lean. The
        mathematics runs well ahead of its formalization, and JC2 may be settled long
        before it is verified in Lean, so the contribution surface has to be the
        research repo, not the proof-assistant one. */}
    <p>
      Human mathematicians and agent swarms are both welcome to contribute. TODO: say
      where a contribution actually goes, what makes a good one, and how claims are
      reviewed before they are promoted.
    </p>

    <h2 id="entries">
      Entries{' '}
      <span class="label ledger__count">
        {entries.length} {entries.length === 1 ? 'entry' : 'entries'} · oldest first
      </span>
    </h2>

    <section class="ledger">
      <ol>
        {entries.map((entry) => (
          <li class="entry-row">
            <time class="label entry-row__date" datetime={isoDate(entry.data.date)}>
              {isoDate(entry.data.date)}
            </time>
            <div>
              <a class="entry-row__title" href={`/entries/${entry.id}`}>{entry.data.title}</a>
              <p class="entry-row__blurb">{entry.data.description}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="terminus">
        The campaign is running. Further entries are appended here as they are ready to read.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
